From c0ae9c3dc0d6f19e3b723ea6fb905aca94ed21a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Les Lee <lesl@google.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 22:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix LOHS BSSID configuration validation bypass

The Local Only Hotspot (LOHS) startup logic was posting the start
request to the WifiHandlerThread. Inside `startSoftApInternal`, which
runs on the handler thread, `Binder.getCallingUid()` and
`Binder.getCallingPid()` were used for validating the SoftApConfiguration.
Because it was running on the handler thread, these calls returned
the system server's identity (SYSTEM_UID), thereby incorrectly passing the
privilege check (which requires NETWORK_SETTINGS) for setting a custom
BSSID.

This change fixes the issue by passing the original LOHS requestor's
calling UID and PID directly to `startSoftApInternal` (which are obtained
on the binder thread when the request is initially received).

Bug: 515051745
Test: atest FrameworksWifiTests:com.android.server.wifi.WifiServiceImplTest#testCustomLohs_BssidValidationFailsForUnprivilegedCaller
Flag: EXEMPT CVE_FIX
Cherrypick-From: https://googleplex-android-review.googlesource.com/q/commit:6dd37bdad465e8995140635a181af5e48cf759b5
Merged-In: Iaeb0be8fc35ad7f8a4fa1c2fb22b1ba7221f8347
Change-Id: Iaeb0be8fc35ad7f8a4fa1c2fb22b1ba7221f8347
